# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROMs, BIOS and firmware — never committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The NewBrain's ROMs are Grundy's, and the COP420 microcode is National's.
# Neither is ours to redistribute. ROMS.txt says what is needed and where it
# goes; the emulator reports plainly when a file is absent.
roms/*
!roms/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tape images — never committed either.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The software library, kept locally for testing. Same rule as the ROMs: none
# of it is ours to redistribute, whatever its licence, so it stays out of the
# repository, out of releases and out of any package. The two files in the
# library that are NOT tape recordings are deliberately absent — Adv's ADV.BIN
# is a raw memory image and Devpac's second half a raw program image, so
# neither can be played into the cassette port.
tapes/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream reference sources, kept locally while porting.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BSD-3-Clause MAME sources, consulted for hardware behaviour. Not ours and
# not needed to build or run this; ATTRIBUTION.md says where to get them.
reference/

# Working files
screen.raw
screen.png
art/src/
node_modules/

# macOS / editor junk
.DS_Store
._*
*~
.claude/
